senses.gloss:
Gaupāyana (‘descendant of Gopa’). The Gaupāyanas
appear in the legend of Asamāti, Kirāta, and Ākuli, which is
first met with in the Brāhmaṇas.^1
1) Pañcaviṃśa Brāhmaṇa, xiii. 12, 5;
Jaiminīva Brāhmaṇa, iii. 167 (Journal
of the American Oriental Society, 18, 41);
Sāṭyāyanaka in Sāyaṇa on Rv. x. 57
(Max Müller's edition, 4^2, c et seq.);
Bṛhaddevatā, vii. 83 et seq., with Mac-
donell's notes.
